{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.GaussianThetaBound","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.GaussianThetaBound","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.GaussianThetaSum"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.abs_tsum_gaussian_sub_sqrt_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.abs_tsum_gaussian_sub_sqrt_le","kind":"theorem","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/GaussianThetaBound.lean#L148-L167","doc":"**The sharp Laplace sum.**  `∑_{n∈ℤ} e^{−a(n−c)²}` is `√(π/a)` — the\nGaussian integral — with a relative error that is exponentially small in `1/a`\nand uniform in the shift `c`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.norm_jacobiTheta₂_sub_one_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.norm_jacobiTheta₂_sub_one_le","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/GaussianThetaBound.lean#L93-L146","doc":"**`θ₂(−c, iπ/a) = 1 + O(e^{−π²/a})`, uniformly in the real shift `c`.**\n\n`S = 0` in `norm_jacobiTheta₂_term_le` because `(-c : ℂ)` has zero imaginary\npart — that is what makes the bound uniform in `c`.  `n² ≥ |n|` then converts\nthe Gaussian tail into a geometric one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.hasSum_int_geometric_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.hasSum_int_geometric_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/GaussianThetaBound.lean#L51-L91","doc":"The two-sided geometric series over `ℤ` with the `n = 0` term removed:\n`∑_{n≠0} q^{|n|} = 2q/(1−q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.jacobiTheta₂_term_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.jacobiTheta₂_term_zero","kind":"theorem","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/GaussianThetaBound.lean#L42-L49","doc":"The `n = 0` term of `θ₂` is `1`, whatever `z` and `τ`.\n\nThe lemma list is spelled out rather than left to `simp`/`norm_num`: with the\ndefault simp set this one goal costs more than the 200000-heartbeat budget,\nfor no reason visible in the statement. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.im_I_mul_pi_div","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.im_I_mul_pi_div","kind":"theorem","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/GaussianThetaBound.lean#L36-L40","doc":"`(iπ/a).im = π/a` — the modulus of the transformed lattice. ","signatureChunk":0}]}